# Quality gate commands (`qualitygate:*`)

Single CLI: `node scripts/qualitygate.mjs` · implementation: `scripts/qualitygate/`.

| npm script | When |
|------------|------|
| `qualitygate:file -- <path>` | After each extract / focused edit (TSC + ESLint + metrics) |
| `qualitygate:changed` | Every **5** completed todos; git-changed `src/**` |
| `qualitygate:capture` | Start fix loop — cache failures → `.local/quality-backlog.md` |
| `qualitygate:backlog` | Show backlog without rescanning |
| `qualitygate:backlog -- done <id>` | Mark one item fixed |
| `qualitygate:metrics` | Full `src/` line + complexity (also end of `npm run typecheck`) |
| `qualitygate:tsc -- --files <path>` | TSC only on files |
| `qualitygate:tsc -- --changed` | TSC only on git-changed |
| `qualitygate:tsc -- --all-slices` | Full partitioned TSC (slow) |
| `qualitygate:tracker -- --skip-tsc` | Refresh `SRC-QUALITY-TRACKER.md` (eslint/magic) |
| `qualitygate:tracker -- --file <path>` | Update one tracker row |

**Many failures?** See `quality-backlog.mdc` — fix one-by-one, rescan every **5** fixes.

**Limits:** 400/800 lines · complexity 15/25 — `code-metrics.mdc`.

**Do not** use removed names: `verify:*`, `quality:*`, `check:code-metrics`, `typecheck:fast`, `tracker:refresh`.
